      "outputs": [],
      "title": "About this workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Keyframe hint, refine and composite\n\nA hint mask on frame 24 is propagated **forwards and backwards** through the clip. In real use, paint the subject on any frame (Load Image → Mask Editor, white = subject) and list that frame in `hint_frames`; several masks take a list such as `0, 48, 120`.\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media.\n\n- **temporal_window**: frames per spatio-temporal attention window. `auto` picks the largest that fits your GPU; `low_vram` stages features through disk with identical results.\n- **Matte Refine, Despill, Composite** run on the keyer's outputs, so changing them does not re-run the model.\n- **coarse_alpha / decision_matte** show the model's internal stage-1 mattes.\n- **Temporal Stability** scores flicker; with a reference matte (here the Demo Clip's true alpha) it also reports SAD, MSE, gradient error and dtSSD."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Keyframe hint, refine and composite\n\nA hint mask on frame 24 is propagated **forwards and backwards** through the clip. In real use, paint the subject on any frame (Load Image → Mask Editor, white = subject) and list that frame in `hint_frames`; several masks take a list such as `0, 48, 120`.\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media.\n\n- **temporal_window**: frames per spatio-temporal attention window. `auto` picks the largest that fits your GPU; `low_vram` stages features through disk with identical results.\n- **Matte Refine, Despill, Composite** run on the keyer's outputs, so changing them does not re-run the model.\n- **coarse_alpha / decision_matte** show the model's internal stage-1 mattes.\n- **Temporal Stability** scores flicker; with a reference matte (here the Demo Clip's true alpha) it also reports SAD, MSE, gradient error and dtSSD."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
